var FEAT_FULL={"Alert": "**Initiative Proficiency.** You may add your Proficiency Bonus to each Initiative roll you make. **Initiative Swap.** Right after you roll Initiative, you can trade Initiative with one willing ally taking part in the same combat. The trade isn't possible if either of you has the Incapacitated condition.", "Crafter": "**Tool Proficiency.** Choose three different Artisan's Tools listed in the Fast Crafting table. You are proficient with each of them. **Discount.** Nonmagical items cost you 20 percent less whenever you buy them. **Fast Crafting.** When you finish a Long Rest, you can make one piece of gear listed in the Fast Crafting table, as long as you have the Artisan's Tools that match it and are proficient with them. The item lasts only until you finish another Long Rest, and then it falls apart. The table pairs each set of tools with the gear it can make. Carpenter's Tools: Ladder, Torch. Leatherworker's Tools: Case, Pouch. Mason's Tools: Block and Tackle. Potter's Tools: Jug, Lamp. Smith's Tools: Ball Bearings, Bucket, Caltrops, Grappling Hook, Iron Pot. Tinker's Tools: Bell, Shovel, Tinder Box. Weaver's Tools: Basket, Rope, Net, Tent. Woodcarver's Tools: Club, Greatclub, Quarterstaff.", "Healer": "**Battle Medic.** While you have a Healer's Kit, you can take a Utilize action to spend one of its uses, tending to a creature within 5 feet of you. That creature can spend one of its Hit Point Dice. You roll the die, and the creature regains Hit Points equal to your Proficiency Bonus plus the result. **Healing Rerolls.** When you roll a die for the Hit Points restored by this feat's Battle Medic benefit or by a spell you cast, you can reroll that die if it comes up 1. You must use the new roll.", "Lucky": "**Luck Points.** Your Proficiency Bonus sets how many Luck Points you have, and you spend them on the benefits below. Finishing a Long Rest restores all the Luck Points you spent. **Advantage.** You can spend 1 Luck Point on any d20 you roll for a D20 Test, which gives you Advantage on that roll. **Disadvantage.** You can spend 1 Luck Point when a creature makes an attack roll against you. If you do, that roll has Disadvantage.", "Magic Initiate (Cleric)": "**Two Cantrips.** Pick two cantrips on the Cleric spell list, and you learn them. When you take this feat, also pick Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma as the spellcasting ability for the spells it gives you. **Level 1 Spell.** Pick a level 1 spell from that same Cleric list. It is always prepared for you. You can cast it once without expending a spell slot, and that free casting returns once you finish a Long Rest. Any spell slots you have can also be used to cast it. **Spell Change.** Each time you gain a level, you can swap one of the spells you picked for this feat for a different spell of the same level from that list. **Repeatable.** You can take this feat more than once, but each time you must pick a different spell list.", "Magic Initiate (Druid)": "**Two Cantrips.** Pick two cantrips on the Druid spell list, and you learn them. When you take this feat, also pick Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma as the spellcasting ability for the spells it gives you. **Level 1 Spell.** Pick a level 1 spell from that same Druid list. It is always prepared for you. You can cast it once without expending a spell slot, and that free casting returns once you finish a Long Rest. Any spell slots you have can also be used to cast it. **Spell Change.** Each time you gain a level, you can swap one of the spells you picked for this feat for a different spell of the same level from that list. **Repeatable.** You can take this feat more than once, but each time you must pick a different spell list.", "Magic Initiate (Wizard)": "**Two Cantrips.** Pick two cantrips on the Wizard spell list, and you learn them. When you take this feat, also pick Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma as the spellcasting ability for the spells it gives you. **Level 1 Spell.** Pick a level 1 spell from that same Wizard list. It is always prepared for you. You can cast it once without expending a spell slot, and that free casting returns once you finish a Long Rest. Any spell slots you have can also be used to cast it. **Spell Change.** Each time you gain a level, you can swap one of the spells you picked for this feat for a different spell of the same level from that list. **Repeatable.** You can take this feat more than once, but each time you must pick a different spell list.", "Musician": "**Instrument Training.** Choose three Musical Instruments. You gain proficiency with them. **Encouraging Song.** Each time you finish a Short or Long Rest, you can perform a song using a Musical Instrument you're proficient with. Allies who hear it gain Heroic Inspiration, up to a number of allies equal to your Proficiency Bonus.", "Savage Attacker": "Your training lets you land especially brutal blows. Once per turn, when your weapon hits a target, you may roll that weapon's damage dice twice and apply whichever roll you prefer to that target.", "Skilled": "Pick three skills or tools, in any mix. You become proficient with each one. **Repeatable.** You may select this feat multiple times.", "Tavern Brawler": "**Enhanced Unarmed Strike.** When your Unarmed Strike hits and deals damage, you can swap its normal damage for Bludgeoning damage of 1d4 plus your Strength modifier. **Damage Rerolls.** If any damage die you roll for your Unarmed Strike shows a 1, you may roll that die again, and the new result must be used. **Improvised Weaponry.** You are proficient with improvised weapons. **Push.** Once per turn, on your turn, when an Unarmed Strike you make as part of the Attack action hits a creature, you can both deal damage and push the creature 5 feet away from you.", "Tough": "When you take this feat, your Hit Point maximum goes up by twice your character level. Each time you gain a character level after that, your Hit Point maximum rises by 2 more Hit Points.", "Ability Score Improvement": "Choose one ability score and raise it by 2, or choose two ability scores and raise each of them by 1. This feat can't push any ability score above 20. **Repeatable.** You can select this feat more than once.", "Actor": "**Ability Score Increase.** Your Charisma score rises by 1, but not above 20. **Impersonation.** While disguised as a real or made-up person, you roll Charisma (Deception or Performance) checks with Advantage when trying to persuade others that you are that person. **Mimicry.** You can imitate the sounds other creatures make, speech included. A creature that hears your imitation can tell it is fake only by passing a Wisdom (Insight) check against DC 8 plus your Charisma modifier and Proficiency Bonus.", "Athlete": "**Ability Score Increase.** Either your Strength or your Dexterity score rises by 1, but not above 20. **Climb Speed.** You have a Climb Speed that matches your Speed. **Hop Up.** While you have the Prone condition, standing back up takes only 5 feet of your movement. **Jumping.** You need to move only 5 feet before making a running Long Jump or High Jump.", "Charger": "**Ability Score Increase.** Either your Strength or your Dexterity score rises by 1, but not above 20. **Improved Dash.** Whenever you take the Dash action, your Speed rises by 10 feet for that action. **Charge Attack.** When a melee attack roll you make during the Attack action hits a target immediately after you move at least 10 feet straight toward it, pick one effect: the attack's damage roll gets a 1d8 bonus, or you push the target up to 10 feet away if its size is at most one size above yours. This benefit works only once on each of your turns.", "Chef": "**Ability Score Increase.** Your Constitution or Wisdom score goes up by 1, up to 20. **Cook's Utensils.** You become proficient with Cook's Utensils if you aren't already. **Replenishing Meal.** During a Short Rest, you can prepare a special meal if you have ingredients and Cook's Utensils with you. The batch feeds a number of creatures equal to your Proficiency Bonus plus 4. When the Short Rest ends, each creature that ate the meal and spends one or more Hit Point Dice to heal gains an additional 1d8 Hit Points. **Bolstering Treats.** With 1 hour of work, or at the end of a Long Rest, you can cook treats, making as many as your Proficiency Bonus, again only with ingredients and Cook's Utensils at hand. The treats stay good for 8 hours after you make them. A creature can eat one as a Bonus Action and gains a number of Temporary Hit Points that matches your Proficiency Bonus.", "Crossbow Expert": "**Ability Score Increase.** Your Dexterity score rises by 1, but not above 20. **Ignore Loading.** The Hand Crossbow, Heavy Crossbow, and Light Crossbow (called crossbows in the rest of this feat) lose the Loading property for you. While you hold one, loading a piece of ammunition into it doesn't require a free hand. **Firing in Melee.** An enemy within 5 feet of you doesn't give you Disadvantage on attack rolls with crossbows. **Dual Wielding.** When you make the extra attack granted by the Light property with a crossbow that has the Light property, you can include your ability modifier in that attack's damage, unless you are already adding it.", "Crusher": "**Ability Score Increase.** Either your Strength or your Constitution score rises by 1, but not above 20. **Push.** Once per turn, when an attack of yours hits a creature and deals Bludgeoning damage, you can move that creature 5 feet into an unoccupied space, as long as its size is at most one size above yours. **Enhanced Critical.** If a Critical Hit you score deals Bludgeoning damage to a creature, any attack roll made against that creature has Advantage until your next turn starts.", "Defensive Duelist": "**Ability Score Increase.** Your Dexterity score rises by 1, but not above 20. **Parry.** When another creature hits you with a melee attack while you hold a Finesse weapon, you can use a Reaction to raise your Armor Class by an amount equal to your Proficiency Bonus, which might make the attack miss. The bonus keeps applying to your Armor Class against melee attacks until your next turn starts.", "Dual Wielder": "**Ability Score Increase.** Either your Strength or your Dexterity score rises by 1, but not above 20. **Enhanced Dual Wielding.** If you take the Attack action on your turn and one of your attacks uses a weapon with the Light property, you can attack one more time later in that same turn as a Bonus Action. This extra attack must use a different weapon, and that weapon must be a Melee weapon that doesn't have the Two-Handed property. The extra attack's damage doesn't include your ability modifier, unless that modifier is negative. **Quick Draw.** Whenever you could normally draw or stow one weapon, you can handle two instead, as long as neither has the Two-Handed property.", "Durable": "**Ability Score Increase.** Your Constitution score rises by 1, but not above 20. **Defy Death.** Your Death Saving Throws have Advantage. **Speedy Recovery.** As a Bonus Action, you can spend one of your Hit Point Dice and roll it, regaining Hit Points equal to the result.", "Elemental Adept": "**Ability Score Increase.** Choose Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma and raise that score by 1, but not above 20. **Energy Mastery.** Pick one damage type: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder. Your spells ignore Resistance to that type. Also, if a spell you cast deals damage of that type, any 1 you roll on that spell's damage dice can be treated as a 2. **Repeatable.** You may select this feat multiple times, but each time you must pick a different damage type for Energy Mastery.", "Fey Touched": "**Ability Score Increase.** Your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma score goes up by 1, up to 20. **Fey Magic.** Pick one level 1 spell of the Divination or Enchantment school. That spell and Misty Step are always prepared for you. You can cast each of them once without expending a spell slot. Once you cast one of them this way, that spell's free casting comes back only when you finish a Long Rest. Either spell can also be cast with spell slots of the appropriate level that you have. The ability you raised with this feat is their spellcasting ability.", "Grappler": "**Ability Score Increase.** Either your Strength or your Dexterity score rises by 1, but not above 20. **Punch and Grab.** Once per turn, when an Unarmed Strike you make as part of the Attack action on your turn hits a creature, you can apply both the Damage option and the Grapple option. **Attack Advantage.** Your attack rolls against a creature you have Grappled have Advantage. **Fast Wrestler.** When you move a creature you have Grappled that is your size or smaller, your Speed isn't halved.", "Great Weapon Master": "**Ability Score Increase.** Your Strength score rises by 1, but not above 20. **Heavy Weapon Mastery.** On your turn, if an attack you make with a Heavy weapon during the Attack action hits a creature, you can make the weapon deal extra damage to the target equal to your Proficiency Bonus. **Hew.** Right after a Melee weapon of yours scores a Critical Hit, or brings a creature down to 0 Hit Points, a Bonus Action lets you make one more attack with that same weapon.", "Heavily Armored": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Constitution or Strength and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Armor Training.** You are now trained to wear Heavy armor.", "Heavy Armor Master": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Constitution or Strength and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Damage Reduction.** When an attack hits you while you wear Heavy armor, any Slashing, Piercing, and Bludgeoning damage it deals you is lowered by your Proficiency Bonus.", "Inspiring Leader": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Wisdom or Charisma and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Bolstering Performance.** Each time a Short or Long Rest ends for you, you can give a stirring performance by delivering a speech, singing a song, or performing a dance. When you do, choose up to six allies within 30 feet of you who witness it, and you can count yourself among them. Each chosen creature gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the modifier of the ability this feat raised plus your character level.", "Keen Mind": "**Ability Score Increase.** Raise your Intelligence by 1 (maximum 20). **Lore Knowledge.** Pick Arcana, History, Investigation, Nature, or Religion. You gain proficiency in that skill, or Expertise in it if you are already proficient. **Quick Study.** The Study action is available to you as a Bonus Action.", "Lightly Armored": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Strength or Dexterity and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Armor Training.** You become trained with Light armor and Shields.", "Mage Slayer": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Strength or Dexterity and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Concentration Breaker.** A concentrating creature you damage has Disadvantage on the saving throw it makes to keep its Concentration. **Guarded Mind.** When you fail an Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma saving throw, you can turn the failure into a success. Once used, this benefit comes back only after you finish a Short or Long Rest.", "Martial Weapon Training": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Strength or Dexterity and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Weapon Proficiency.** You are now proficient with Martial weapons.", "Medium Armor Master": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Strength or Dexterity and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Dexterous Wearer.** If your Dexterity score is 16 or higher, you can add 3 instead of 2 to your Armor Class while you wear Medium armor.", "Moderately Armored": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Strength or Dexterity and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Armor Training.** You become trained with Medium armor.", "Mounted Combatant": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Strength, Dexterity, or Wisdom and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Mounted Strike.** As long as you are mounted, your attack rolls have Advantage against a creature that isn't mounted, if it is within 5 feet of your mount and at least one size smaller than the mount. **Leap Aside.** When an effect offers your mount a Dexterity saving throw that halves the damage, the mount instead takes no damage on a success and only half damage on a failure. Your mount gets this benefit only while you ride it and neither of you has the Incapacitated condition. **Veer.** While you are mounted and lack the Incapacitated condition, you can make an attack that hits your mount hit you instead.", "Observant": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Intelligence or Wisdom and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Keen Observer.** Pick Insight, Investigation, or Perception. You gain proficiency in that skill, or Expertise in it if you are already proficient. **Quick Search.** The Search action is available to you as a Bonus Action.", "Piercer": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Strength or Dexterity and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Puncture.** Once per turn, if an attack of yours that deals Piercing damage hits a creature, you can reroll one of its damage dice and must keep the new result. **Enhanced Critical.** If a Critical Hit you score against a creature deals Piercing damage, you can roll one more damage die when working out the extra Piercing damage the target takes.", "Poisoner": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Dexterity or Intelligence and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Potent Poison.** Resistance to Poison damage doesn't reduce your damage rolls that deal Poison damage. **Brew Poison.** The Poisoner's Kit becomes one of your proficiencies. Working 1 hour with the kit, plus 50 GP spent on materials, yields doses of poison equal in number to your Proficiency Bonus. A Bonus Action lets you coat a weapon or a piece of ammunition with a dose. The poison on it lasts 1 minute or until you hit with that item, whichever comes first. A creature that takes damage from the coated item makes a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus the modifier of the ability this feat increased. On a failed save, it takes 2d8 Poison damage and is Poisoned until your next turn ends.", "Polearm Master": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Strength or Dexterity and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Pole Strike.** Once you have taken the Attack action and made an attack with a Spear, a Quarterstaff, or a weapon with both the Reach and Heavy properties, you can immediately spend a Bonus Action on a melee attack with the weapon's opposite end. That attack deals Bludgeoning damage and uses a d4 as its damage die. **Reactive Strike.** If you are holding a Spear, a Quarterstaff, or a weapon with both the Reach and Heavy properties, you can take a Reaction when a creature enters your reach with that weapon, making one melee attack against it.", "Resilient": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick an ability whose saving throw you aren't proficient in. That score increases by 1 (maximum 20). **Saving Throw Proficiency.** From now on, you are proficient in saving throws of that ability.", "Ritual Caster": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Ritual Spells.** Pick level 1 spells with the Ritual tag, as many as your Proficiency Bonus. They are always prepared for you, and you can cast them using any of your spell slots. The ability this feat increased is their spellcasting ability. Each time your Proficiency Bonus goes up after that, you can choose one more level 1 Ritual-tagged spell, and this feat keeps it always prepared too. **Quick Ritual.** This benefit lets you cast a Ritual spell you have prepared with its normal casting time instead of the longer Ritual time, and no spell slot is spent. After using it, you must finish a Long Rest before using it again.", "Sentinel": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick Strength or Dexterity and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Guardian.** You can make an Opportunity Attack against a creature within 5 feet of you immediately after it takes the Disengage action or after it hits a target other than you with an attack. **Halt.** If an Opportunity Attack of yours hits a creature, that creature's Speed becomes 0 until the current turn ends.", "Shadow Touched": "**Ability Score Increase.** Your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma score goes up by 1, up to 20. **Shadow Magic.** Pick a level 1 spell of the Illusion or Necromancy school. That spell and Invisibility are always prepared for you. You can cast each of the two once with no spell slot. Once you use that free casting for one of them, it returns for that spell only when you finish a Long Rest. You may also cast either one with spell slots of the right level that you have. The ability raised by this feat is their spellcasting ability.", "Sharpshooter": "**Ability Score Increase.** Raise your Dexterity by 1 (maximum 20). **Bypass Cover.** Three-Quarters Cover and Half Cover give no protection against ranged attacks you make with weapons. **Firing in Melee.** Your attack rolls with Ranged weapons don't have Disadvantage because an enemy is within 5 feet of you. **Long Shots.** Your attack rolls with Ranged weapons also don't have Disadvantage when you attack at long range.", "Shield Master": "**Ability Score Increase.** Your Strength score goes up by 1, up to 20. **Shield Bash.** When you use the Attack action to attack a creature within 5 feet of you and hit it with a Melee weapon, you can strike it right away with your Shield, as long as the Shield is equipped. It makes a Strength saving throw against a DC equal to 8 plus your Strength modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus. On a failed save, you either push it 5 feet away from you or give it the Prone condition, whichever you choose. You can do this only once on each of your turns. **Interpose Shield.** While you hold a Shield, an effect may let you make a Dexterity saving throw to reduce its damage by half. In that case, you can take a Reaction so that a successful saving throw leaves you with no damage at all.", "Skill Expert": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick one ability score and raise it by 1 (maximum 20). **Skill Proficiency.** Choose any skill and become proficient in it. **Expertise.** Pick a skill you're already proficient in that doesn't have Expertise yet, and gain Expertise in it.", "Skulker": "**Ability Score Increase.** Your Dexterity rises by 1 (maximum 20). **Blindsight.** You gain Blindsight out to 10 feet. **Fog of War.** The chaos of battle helps you disappear: during combat, you have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made when you take the Hide action. **Sniper.** When you attack while hidden and miss, the attack roll doesn't give away where you are.", "Slasher": "**Ability Score Increase.** Add 1 to your Strength or Dexterity (maximum 20). **Hamstring.** When an attack of yours hits a creature and deals Slashing damage, you can cut that creature's Speed by 10 feet until your next turn starts (once per turn). **Enhanced Critical.** If your Critical Hit against a creature deals Slashing damage, it makes attack rolls with Disadvantage until your next turn starts.", "Speedy": "**Ability Score Increase.** Add 1 to your Dexterity or Constitution (maximum 20). **Speed Increase.** You gain 10 extra feet of Speed. **Dash over Difficult Terrain.** If you take the Dash action during your turn, Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement until that turn ends. **Agile Movement.** Any Opportunity Attack against you has Disadvantage.", "Spell Sniper": "**Ability Score Increase.** Add 1 to your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (maximum 20). **Bypass Cover.** Your spell attack rolls ignore Three-Quarters Cover as well as Half Cover. **Casting in Melee.** Having an enemy within 5 feet of you doesn't give you Disadvantage on spell attack rolls. **Increased Range.** If a spell you cast needs an attack roll and its range is 10 feet or more, you can extend that range by 60 feet.", "Telekinetic": "**Ability Score Increase.** Add 1 to your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (maximum 20). **Minor Telekinesis.** You learn Mage Hand. When you cast it, you may leave out its Verbal and Somatic components, turn the spectral hand Invisible, and add 30 feet to its range. You cast it with the ability this feat raised. **Telekinetic Shove.** Using a Bonus Action, you can give one creature within 30 feet that you can see a telekinetic shove. It makes a Strength saving throw against a DC of 8 + your Proficiency Bonus + the modifier of the ability this feat raised. On a failure, you shift it 5 feet closer to you or farther away.", "Telepathic": "**Ability Score Increase.** Add 1 to your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (maximum 20). **Telepathic Utterance.** You can project telepathic speech to any creature within 60 feet that you can see. The message uses a language you know, so the creature can understand it only if it shares that language. This benefit gives it no way to answer you telepathically. **Detect Thoughts.** The Detect Thoughts spell is always prepared for you. You can cast it with no spell slot and no spell components, and once you do, that free casting returns only after you finish a Long Rest. You can also cast it by expending spell slots of the right level that you have. For this spell, your spellcasting ability is the one this feat raised.", "War Caster": "**Ability Score Increase.** Add 1 to your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (maximum 20). **Concentration.** When you make a Constitution saving throw to keep your Concentration, you have Advantage on it. **Reactive Spell.** If a creature provokes your Opportunity Attack by leaving your reach, you may instead use your Reaction to target it with a spell. The spell must take one action to cast and must have that creature as its only target. **Somatic Components.** Even with weapons or a Shield occupying one or both hands, you can still perform Somatic components when casting spells.", "Weapon Master": "**Ability Score Increase.** Add 1 to your Strength or Dexterity (maximum 20). **Mastery Property.** Choose a kind of weapon, Simple or Martial, that you have proficiency with. Your weapon training lets you use the mastery property of that kind of weapon. After each Long Rest, you can swap your choice for another eligible kind.", "Archery": "Any attack roll you make with a Ranged weapon gains a +2 bonus.", "Blind Fighting": "You gain Blindsight out to 10 feet.", "Defense": "Your Armor Class gets a +1 bonus while you have Light, Medium, or Heavy armor on.", "Dueling": "If the only weapon you're holding is a Melee weapon held in one hand, your damage rolls with it gain a +2 bonus.", "Great Weapon Fighting": "On damage rolls for attacks with a Melee weapon you hold in two hands, you can count a 1 or 2 on any damage die as a 3. This requires a weapon with the Versatile or Two-Handed property.", "Interception": "If a creature you can see makes an attack roll that hits someone else within 5 feet of you, you can use a Reaction to reduce the damage that target takes by 1d10 plus your Proficiency Bonus. This Reaction requires you to be holding a Shield, a Simple weapon, or a Martial weapon.", "Protection": "If you hold a Shield, you can take a Reaction to interpose it whenever a creature you can see makes an attack against someone else who stands within 5 feet of you. The triggering attack roll has Disadvantage, and so does every other attack roll against that target until the start of your next turn, as long as you stay within 5 feet of it.", "Thrown Weapon Fighting": "When a ranged attack roll you make with a weapon bearing the Thrown property hits, add a +2 bonus to its damage roll.", "Two-Weapon Fighting": "When the Light property of a weapon gives you an extra attack, you may include your ability modifier in that attack's damage, unless you already add it.", "Unarmed Fighting": "When your Unarmed Strike hits and deals damage, you can replace its normal damage with Bludgeoning damage of 1d6 plus your Strength modifier. Roll a d8 instead of the d6 if you're holding no weapons and no Shield as you make the attack roll. When each of your turns begins, you can choose one creature you have Grappled and deal 1d4 Bludgeoning damage to it.", "Blessed Warrior": "Choose two cantrips from the Cleric spell list and learn them. Guidance and Sacred Flame are recommended. For you, they count as Paladin spells, and they use Charisma as your spellcasting ability. Each time you gain a Paladin level, you can swap one of them for a different Cleric cantrip.", "Druidic Warrior": "Choose two cantrips from the Druid spell list and learn them. Guidance and Starry Wisp are recommended. For you, they count as Ranger spells, and they use Wisdom as your spellcasting ability. Each time you gain a Ranger level, you can swap one of them for a different Druid cantrip.", "Boon of Combat Prowess": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick one ability score and raise it by 1 (maximum 30). **Peerless Aim.** If you miss with an attack roll, you can choose to hit instead. After you use this benefit, it's unavailable until your next turn starts.", "Boon of Dimensional Travel": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick one ability score and raise it by 1 (maximum 30). **Blink Steps.** Immediately after taking the Magic action or the Attack action, you can teleport to an unoccupied space you can see up to 30 feet away.", "Boon of Energy Resistance": "**Ability Score Increase.** Pick one ability score and raise it by 1 (maximum 30). **Energy Resistances.** Choose two damage types from Acid, Fire, Cold, Thunder, Lightning, Necrotic, Radiant, Poison, and Psychic. You have Resistance to both, and you can swap your picks each time you finish a Long Rest. **Energy Redirection.** If damage of one of your chosen types hits you, you can use a Reaction to redirect damage of that type at a different creature within 60 feet that you can see and that isn't behind Total Cover. That creature attempts a Dexterity saving throw against a DC of 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Constitution modifier, and on a failure it takes damage of that type equal to 2d12 plus your Constitution modifier.", "Boon of Fate": "**Ability Score Increase.** Choose an ability score and add 1 to it (maximum 30). **Improve Fate.** When a D20 Test made by you or by another creature within 60 feet of you succeeds or fails, you can roll 2d4 and apply the total to that d20 roll as either a bonus or a penalty. After using this benefit, you must roll Initiative or finish a Short or Long Rest before you can use it again.", "Boon of Fortitude": "**Ability Score Increase.** Choose an ability score and add 1 to it (maximum 30). **Fortified Health.** Add 40 to your Hit Point maximum. Also, each time you regain Hit Points, you can regain extra Hit Points equal to your Constitution modifier. After you gain this extra healing, it isn't available again until your next turn begins.", "Boon of Irresistible Offense": "**Ability Score Increase.** Add 1 to your Strength or Dexterity score (maximum 30). **Overcome Defenses.** Your Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage always bypasses Resistance. **Overwhelming Strike.** Whenever the d20 of your attack roll shows a 20, you can deal the target bonus damage equal to the score of the ability you raised with this feat. The bonus damage uses the attack's damage type.", "Boon of Recovery": "**Ability Score Increase.** Choose an ability score and add 1 to it (maximum 30). **Last Stand.** If you would be brought to 0 Hit Points, you have the option to go to 1 Hit Point instead and then regain Hit Points equal to half your Hit Point maximum. This benefit is then unavailable until you finish a Long Rest. **Recover Vitality.** You keep a pool of ten d10s. You can spend dice from this pool as a Bonus Action, rolling them and regaining Hit Points equal to the total rolled. All spent dice return to the pool when you finish a Long Rest.", "Boon of Skill": "**Ability Score Increase.** Choose an ability score and add 1 to it (maximum 30). **All-Around Adept.** You are proficient in every skill. **Expertise.** Pick one skill you don't already have Expertise in, and gain Expertise in it.", "Boon of Speed": "**Ability Score Increase.** Choose an ability score and add 1 to it (maximum 30). **Escape Artist.** You can use a Bonus Action to take the Disengage action. When you do, the Grappled condition also ends on you. **Quickness.** Add 30 feet to your Speed.", "Boon of Spell Recall": "**Ability Score Increase.** Add 1 to your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma score (maximum 30). **Free Casting.** Whenever you use a spell slot of level 1 to 4 to cast a spell, roll 1d4. If the roll equals the slot's level, you don't expend the slot.", "Boon of the Night Spirit": "**Ability Score Increase.** Choose an ability score and add 1 to it (maximum 30). **Merge with Shadows.** While you are in Dim Light or Darkness, a Bonus Action lets you give yourself the Invisible condition. The condition ends right after you take any action, Bonus Action, or Reaction. **Shadowy Form.** Whenever Dim Light or Darkness surrounds you, you have Resistance to every damage type except Psychic and Radiant.", "Boon of Truesight": "**Ability Score Increase.** Choose an ability score and add 1 to it (maximum 30). **Truesight.** You gain Truesight out to 60 feet."};

var HEIGHT={Aasimar:{Medium:[4,7],Small:[2,4]},Dragonborn:{Medium:[5,7]},Dwarf:{Medium:[4,5]},Elf:{Medium:[5,6]},Gnome:{Small:[3,4]},Goliath:{Medium:[7,8]},Halfling:{Small:[2,3]},Human:{Medium:[4,7],Small:[2,4]},Orc:{Medium:[6,7]},Tiefling:{Medium:[4,7],Small:[2,4]}};
